.TH ARC 1 "November 2026" "FreeArc-c 1.4.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arc \- FreeArc high-compression archive manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arc
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIarchive\fR[\fI.arc\fR] [\fIfiles...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arc
is a modern native C/C++ implementation of the FreeArc archiver. It provides
high compression ratios through advanced algorithms (LZMA, PPMD, GRZip, Tornado,
TTA) combined with intelligent preprocessors (REP, DICT, DELTA, BCJ/EXE, MM, LZP).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B a, add, c, create
Add files to archive (default).
.TP
.B u, update
Update newer files and add new files.
.TP
.B f, freshen
Freshen existing files in archive (no new files added).
.TP
.B d, delete
Delete files or patterns from archive.
.TP
.B m, move
Move files to archive (delete from disk after archiving).
.TP
.B l, list
Display archive file listing.
.TP
.B v
Display verbose archive file listing with Unix attributes and CRCs.
.TP
.B t, test
Test archive integrity.
.TP
.B e
Extract files without pathnames.
.TP
.B x, extract
Extract files with pathnames.
.TP
.B p
Extract files to standard output (pipe).
.TP
.B s
Convert an existing archive to a standalone self-extracting executable (SFX).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m \ METHOD
Select compression method, level, or filter chain (e.g. \fBstoring\fR, \fBlzma\fR, \fBtor\fR, \fBppmd\fR, \fBgrzip\fR, \fBtta\fR, \fB-m0\fR..\fB-m9\fR, \fB-mx\fR, \fB-m1x\fR..\fB-m9x\fR, \fB-m exe+lzma\fR).
.TP
.B \-bcj
Activate x86 executable branch filter (alias: \fB-exe\fR).
.TP
.B \-rep
Activate repetition filter (\fBrep:64m\fR).
.TP
.B \-delta
Activate delta filter.
.TP
.B \-dict
Activate dictionary filter.
.TP
.B \-lzp
Activate LZP filter.
.TP
.B \-mm
Activate multimedia filter.
.TP
.B \-sfx\fR[\fB=\fISTUB\fR]
Create a standalone self-extracting executable (.sfx or .run).
.TP
.B \-s\fR, \fB\-s-
Create solid archive (default) or non-solid archive (one data block per file).
.TP
.BI \-s SIZE
Set solid block size limit (e.g. \fB-s64m\fR).
.TP
.BI \-s N\fRf
Set solid block limit by file count (e.g. \fB-s10f\fR).
.TP
.B \-r\fR, \fB\-r-
Recurse subdirectories (default) or disable recursion.
.TP
.B \-p \fIPASS\fR, \fB\-hp \fIPASS
Encrypt data blocks (\fB-p\fR) or headers and data (\fB-hp\fR) with password.
.TP
.BI \-ae \ ALG
Encryption algorithm: \fBaes\fR (default), \fBaes-128\fR, \fBaes-256\fR, \fBblowfish\fR, \fBtwofish\fR, or \fBserpent\fR.
.TP
.BI \-v SIZE
Create multi-volume archive (e.g. \fB-v10m\fR, \fB-v1440k\fR).
.TP
.BI \-x \ PATTERN\fR,\ \fB\-i \ PATTERN
Exclude (\fB-x\fR) or include only (\fB-i\fR) files matching pattern (\fB@listfile\fR supported).
.TP
.B \-so
Write extracted files to stdout.
.TP
.B \-ep\fR, \fB\-ep1
Store basenames only (\fB-ep\fR) or strip the first path component (\fB-ep1\fR).
.TP
.BI \-ap \ PATH
Set archive path prefix.
.TP
.BI \-z \ TEXT
Set archive comment (or \fB-zFILE\fR to read from a file).
.TP
.BI \-dp \ DIR\fR,\ \fB\-\-diskpath= DIR
Set base disk path for compression/extraction.
.TP
.BI \-ld \ MEM
Limit memory usage for decompression (e.g. \fB-ld64m\fR, \fB--LimitDecompMem=64m\fR).
.TP
.BI \-lc \ MEM
Limit memory usage for compression (e.g. \fB-lc256m\fR, \fB--LimitCompMem=256m\fR).
.TP
.BI \-lo \ FILE\fR,\ \fB\-\-logfile= FILE
Mirror all console output, progress, and errors to file.
.TP
.BI \-mt \ NUM\fR,\ \fB\-\-multithreaded= NUM
Set number of worker threads.
.TP
.B \-q\fR, \fB\-\-noarcext
Enable quiet mode (\fB-q\fR) or avoid appending \fB.arc\fR to the archive name (\fB--noarcext\fR).
.TP
.BI \-cfg FILE\fR,\ \fB\-\-config= FILE\fR,\ \fB\-cfg-\fR,\ \fB\-\-no-config\fR,\ \fB\-\-print-config
Specify, disable, or inspect active \fBarc.ini\fR configuration.
.TP
.B \-nobitexact\fR, \fB\-\-max-ratio
Maximize compression ratio while remaining format-compatible with legacy \fBunarc 0.67\fR.
.TP
.BI \-mc= N\fR,\ \fB\-fb= N
Override LZMA match finder search cycles (\fB16..1000\fR) and fast bytes (\fB32..273\fR).
.TP
.BI @ LIST
Read file paths from \fILIST\fR (one path per line).
.SH AUTHOR
Modern native C/C++ port by seb3773. Original FreeArc format by Bulat Ziganshin.
